    "fullText": "Hand-Gesture Python Game Automation (Windows)\nControl a game’s acceleration and braking using your hand gestures via your webcam. This app detects your hand with MediaPipe and injects keyboard inputs on Windows with the low-level SendInput API for responsive gameplay.\n\nFeatures\nWebcam Hand Tracking: Uses MediaPipe Hands to detect fingers up/down in real time.\nGesture-to-Key Mapping:\n0 fingers = Brake (Left Arrow)\n5 fingers = Gas (Right Arrow)\nGame-Friendly Input: Sends hardware scan codes via Windows SendInput (more reliable for games).\nCustomizable Controls: Easily change gestures and key mappings.\nDemo\nHand Landmarks\n\nRequirements\nOperating System: Windows 10/11\nPython: 3.8+\nHardware: Webcam\nPython Packages:\nopencv-python\nmediapipe\nInstallation\nInstall Python 3.8 or higher.\nInstall required packages:\npip install opencv-python mediapipe\nClone this repository:\ngit clone https://github.com/Suhas-Ramesha/Hand-Gesture-Python-Game.git\ncd Hand-Gesture-Python-Game\nRun the app:\npython main.py\nQuick Start\nGive the app a few seconds to start the webcam.\nFace your palm to the camera with good lighting.\nPress q to quit.\nControls (Default)\n0 fingers up: Brake → sends Left Arrow (scan code 0x4B)\n5 fingers up: Gas → sends Right Arrow (scan code 0x4D)\nYou can change these mappings in main.py.\n\nHow It Works\nHand Tracking (MediaPipe)\nCaptures frames from your webcam with OpenCV.\nRuns MediaPipe Hands to detect a single hand and its 21 landmarks.\nDetermines which fingers are “up” by comparing fingertip positions to their lower joints:\nThumb: compares x-positions.\nOther fingers: compares y-positions of tip vs. proximal joints.\nGesture Mapping\nCounts the number of fingers up:\ntotal == 0 → Brake\ntotal == 5 → Gas\nDraws an on-screen label (“BRAKE” or “GAS”) when active.\nKeyboard Injection (Windows SendInput)\ndirectkeys.py recreates Windows INPUT/KEYBDINPUT structs via ctypes.\nSends hardware scan codes with SendInput:\nPress: KEYEVENTF_SCANCODE (0x0008)\nRelease: KEYEVENTF_SCANCODE | KEYEVENTF_KEYUP (0x0008 | 0x0002)\nDefaults:\nleft_pressed = 0x4B (Left Arrow)\nright_pressed = 0x4D (Right Arrow)\nUsing scan codes is layout-agnostic and often accepted by games.\nCustomization\nChange Gestures\nEdit the finger-count logic in main.py to map other counts (1–4) to different actions.\nChange Keys\nIn directkeys.py, update or add scan codes.\nSet your desired keys in main.py.\nTip: For WASD, e.g., W is scan code 0x11 (US layout).\nTroubleshooting\nNothing Happens In-Game:\nRun the script as Administrator.\nSome games/anti-cheat block injected input.\nArrow Keys Not Recognized:\nArrows are “extended” keys. Add KEYEVENTF_EXTENDEDKEY (0x0001) to dwFlags for those keys in directkeys.py.\nCamera Issues:\nEnsure only one app uses the webcam.\nImprove lighting, keep your hand within frame.\nFalse Positives:\nAdjust finger logic or require a gesture to be stable for a few frames before triggering.\nSafety and Fair Use\nUse responsibly. Some games prohibit automation or injected inputs. Respect game ToS and local rules.\n\nAcknowledgements\nMediaPipe Hands for real-time hand landmark detection.\nOpenCV for camera capture and drawing.\nWinAPI SendInput for low-level input injection on Windows.",
